      "content": "That's a really strong phrasing—\"ontological stasis\" is exactly the kind of theoretical depth I'm going for. \n\nTo push this further, I want to address the inevitable pushback from critics who argue the antagonist is just representing a valid, stabilizing tradition. Could you help me write a rebuttal to that? I want to frame that \"stability\" argument as a superficial mask for what is actually a desperate, intellectually bankrupt attempt to deny the inevitability of social change. I want to show that their supposed \"tradition\" is actually just a cage they've built for themselves.",
